<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!-- New native content, SYSTECH_ELECTRIC_BOLT_1 (not absorbed — RSW_ prefix per
     design/NAMING_SCHEME_PLAN.md). The Systech Static Blaster's replacement
     projectile: the donor's KotORElectricBolt needed an AthenaPort class we
     never absorbed and must never re-add (see the item file). Repointing the
     weapon to the existing KotORIonBolt_default kept it firing but made it
     visually and mechanically identical to its three ion-pistol siblings in
     the same file — an ion bolt's EMP extra damage is a droid-only effect,
     wasted on the organic creature (a veermok) the weapon's own fluff names.

     Same base as KotORIonBolt_default (guy762_BaseBullet_VehicleDamageReducer)
     and same order of magnitude damage, so this is a flavour/identity fix, not
     a rebalance — Systech's overall power is left where WEAPONS_DONOR_RETIREMENT_1
     put it. A real damage-tier pass for this weapon (if the owner wants it to
     hit like a real anti-creature weapon rather than a near-zero verb weapon,
     per this mod's own "the verb IS the weapon" doctrine) is a separate, larger
     call this item was not asked to make.

     Zero new art: Weapons/Projectiles/zap.png already ships in this mod's own
     Textures folder and is a lightning-bolt sprite no def in the pack
     references (checked: only zapbeam_blue and setforSTUN are wired to
     anything). Same zero-art-cost reuse pattern as RSW_Sonic_Cannon.xml. -->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="guy762_BaseBullet_VehicleDamageReducer">
    <defName>RSW_ElectricArcBolt_default</defName>
    <label>electric arc</label>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Weapons/Projectiles/zap</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <shaderType>TransparentPostLight</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <projectile>
      <damageDef>RSW_RangedDamage_electrical</damageDef>
      <damageAmountBase>8</damageAmountBase>
      <armorPenetrationBase>0.05</armorPenetrationBase>
      <speed>50</speed>
    </projectile>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
